Title: GHETTO SUBURBS
Credit: Written by
Author: Joshua Odiase
Contact: joshuaodiase1@gmail.com

INT. TACO BELL - KITCHEN - NIGHT

MANI (22), skinny but defined, with a fro, African American. His head struggles to stay upright as it drifts downward, eye bags protruding, eyelids flickering to stay open.

CUSTOMER (O.S.)
I would like a Nachos BellGrande with a large Freeze.

Mani jolts when he realizes a customer is in the drive-thru. He quickly prepares the order, reads him his total, and hands off the food.

The clock strikes 2 A.M. Mani grabs a coffee, which only slightly picks up his lethargic movements -- then he hears a ROARING V12 MUSCLE CAR and looks up to see a sideshow in the parking lot.

Later. The clock strikes 8 A.M. Mani sluggishly grabs his paycheck off the wall and grabs his backpack, then slowly makes his way to the back to quickly make himself three Supreme Burritos and a Freeze.

EXT. TACO BELL - PARKING LOT - MORNING

Mani leaves the restaurant. He reaches for the wired earphones in his pocket, connects them to his phone, and plays "American Tterroristt" by RXKNephew. He walks by a gas station encased in police tape.

EXT. WEALTHY CUL-DE-SAC - MORNING

Mani walks keenly through a neighborhood of similar model one- and two-story homes, sprinklers trickling on the lawns in unison. He walks by a pole with a Neighborhood Watch sign.

CUT TO:

EXT. IMPOVERISHED NEIGHBORHOOD - MORNING

Mani walks through his own neighborhood: littered streets, glass shards on the ground, destitute houses with withered lawns and weeds. A "Vote for [Mayor]" sign on one of the lawns. Homeless people talk to themselves in raggedy clothing. A car with its tires taken has the words "STOP CALLING THE COPS ON MY CARS FAGGOTS!!!" spelled in the dust.

Kids play basketball in the street.

NEIGHBORHOOD KID
Check up.

A pimped-out convertible ZOOMS down the street playing MIKE SHERM. Mani swivels his head to see the car coming fast -- almost hitting the group of kids. The kids hastily grab the ball and run to the sidewalk.

NEIGHBORHOOD KID (CONT'D)
AYE!!

As Mani walks past the kids, he sees his neighbor's M3 parking up against a Dodge Charger. He reaches the front door of his impoverished but quaint project housing, stops, and notices a newspaper on his doorstep. He picks it up.

INT. MANI'S HOUSE - MORNING

Mani opens the door and steps inside, casually skimming the newspaper while humming. He sets the newspaper and his paycheck down on the counter and heads to the fridge, only to find it scarcely stocked with fruit and frozen packaged food.

ALICIA (21), messy curly hair, African American, slim but curvy, methodically looks over at Mani. Their daughter, CELINE (4), curly hair, sits in Alicia's arms watching The Powerpuff Girls. Alicia slowly gets up without attracting Celine's attention.

Mani scans the fridge, irritated by the lack of food. As he sets his smuggled food inside, he makes strong eye contact with Alicia, who is holding up his paycheck.

ALICIA
So....

MANI
Save it. Not trynna hear that right now.

ALICIA
(whispers)
Well, you're gonna.

Alicia opens a children's Disney book and shows him a page with a dick drawn inside.

ALICIA (CONT'D)
Can you tell me what shouldn't be here?

MANI
The fuck is this.

ALICIA
That's what I should be saying, because you didn't bother to check the damn pages.

MANI
Why would I check the fucking pages expecting that shit?

ALICIA
Not would... should have.

MANI
What you want me to do.

Alicia moves on from the conversation and starts to wave the check.

ALICIA
(eager)
How much?

MANI
Not enough.

Mani closes the fridge.

ALICIA
(mouthing)
Fuck.

She glances behind her to make sure her daughter didn't hear.

ALICIA (CONT'D)
You have to quit.

MANI
(sarcastically)
And go somewhere else that will pay me 50 cents more to put up with more bullshit?

Celine goes to open the fridge.

CELINE
Mommy, do we have Go-Gurt, like at Jenny's house?

ALICIA
Sorry, sweetheart. We don't.

CELINE
(frustrated)
Why?

ALICIA
Cavities. You know how you don't like going to the dentist.

CELINE
Uh-huh.

ALICIA
Well, eating that will land your butt right back in that chair.

CELINE
(sad)
Okay.

MANI
W-

ALICIA
(interrupting)
Don't.

Alicia hands Mani a letter. He opens it inquisitively and reads hesitantly.

MANI
Private tutor?

ALICIA
She's falling behind her classmates in reading.

MANI
Okay... I'll start reading to her.

ALICIA
How... when you're cooking up freezer tacos all day? And that's not even the main problem. She needs new books.

MANI
What's wrong with the one I got at the book drive?

Alicia takes the book from beside Celine and flips through it to show Mani the dick page again.

MANI
(turning to other pages)
I mean... it got Disney princesses, magic, romance...

Alicia opens the book to the dick drawing once more, looking at Mani sardonically.

MANI
Well, new books cost a good 15, 20 each, along with everything else.

ALICIA
Maybe I can ask Rob if I can pick up more shifts at work.

MANI
Even if the perv would, who would watch Celine then?

ALICIA
What about your mom?

MANI
Working the nursery. What about yours?

Alicia shakes her head.

MANI
(ironically smiling)
Still pulling that bullshit.

They both look at their daughter watching TV.

ALICIA
(dejected; getting emotional)
Look at her. She doesn't deserve this.

Mani comes up behind Alicia, wraps his arms around her abdomen, and rests his head on her shoulder, kissing her temple to comfort her. Celine notices and rushes energetically to comfort her mother.

CELINE
Mommy, what's wrong?

ALICIA
It's nothing, sweetie.

CELINE
Okay. Are we still going for ice cream?!

Alicia, taken aback by the request, crouches down to Celine's eye level.

ALICIA
We definitely are!

She looks aggressively at Mani, who looks vexed by the situation.

CELINE
You forgot, didn't you?

ALICIA
No, sweetie! We'll go. Right?

She looks intensely back at Mani.

MANI
...Right. We promise, but later.

CELINE
(disappointed)
Do you really promise?

Mani crouches down to Celine and sticks out his pinky.

MANI
You see this? When we interlock our fingers, I can't break my promise.

CELINE
Really? Okay. If you don't come or forget, you broke your promise.

MANI
I won't.

ALICIA
He won't.

Alicia looks coldly at Mani.

MANI
(changing his voice)
You know, it's getting stuffy in here. Let's go get some sun, shall we?

CELINE
Shall we what?

MANI
(bowing)
Shall we... your highness. I'll be your chariot to your humble destination, your excellency.

Celine hops onto Mani's back.

CELINE
Yeah!

MANI
(running out the door)
Onward!

Alicia walks after them.

EXT. THE PLAYLOT - NOON

Alicia, smoking a joint, looks fondly at Mani and Celine playing basketball. After Celine makes a shot, they come toward each other, and Celine throws jabs at Mani's hands like a boxer-trainer duo.

MANI
Damn!! Float like a butterfly...

CELINE
Sting like a beeeee!

MANI
Aye, almost forgot.

Mani gives her a bottle of bubbles.

CELINE
Thank youuu.

She hugs Mani tightly for a quick second, then starts blowing bubbles next to Mani and Alicia.

ALICIA
Mani.

Alicia holds up his phone, showing he got a notification.

INT. MS. G'S HOUSE - DAY

JB (22), Filipino, perm fade, tattoos, comes in and closes the front door, looking at his phone. He sees bills and court notices on the counter and nudgingly picks them up with one hand; his other hand holds a bag. He sees MS. G (47), Filipina, short, long black-and-white hair.

MS. G
Oh, JB, did you get the candles?

JB
(handing the candles out of the bag)
Yeah.

MS. G
Thank you.

JB
Gotchu, Ms. G.

JB walks up the stairs and sees JB'S MOTHER (early 40s), Filipina, short, concertedly praying to a statue of Mary with a cross in her clasped hands. He goes to his brother, MARS (14), around the same height as JB, in the gaming room playing FIFA.

NOTE: All dialogue in [brackets] is spoken in Tagalog.

MARS
[Aye JB, when we gonna run it? You been ducking!]

JB
[You know I only play with stakes.]

MARS
How about the cookies in the fridge.

JB
(chuckles)
You serious. Maybe later.

MARS
Bitch made. Sad to see.

JB
Bitch? When you start talkin like that?

MARS
Been sayin that.

JB
Keep sayin it and Mom gonna whoop yo ass.

MARS
(pestering)
I got that handled. So you going to play or go out like a bitch?

JB
Not now... later.

MARS
Swear.

JB
Swear to God.

MARS
You said on God, so no going back.

JB
It's crazy you saying that but don't know a Bible verse.

MARS
I know a verse.

JB looks at Mars, waiting.

MARS (CONT'D)
John 3:16. For God so loved the world, he... gave...

A beat. JB looks at him in pity and walks away while Mars is still talking.

MARS (O.S.)
Aye, where you going?

JB walks to his room. On top of his drawer sits a newspaper, highlighted and tattooed with notes, next to a miniature Jesus figurine.

He crouches down to the drawer, which holds unground weed in a Ziploc bag; he lays it on the desk alongside a condom. A stack of wadded cash -- he picks it up, looks at it as if in a trance, then puts it back. He takes out a 9mm pistol and holsters it at his belt, covering it with his shirt.

He peeks outside his door to see his mother standing up from her prayer. JB gets up off his knees one at a time, quickly puts the weed and newspaper in his bag, closes the drawer, checks his phone, and walks out toward his mother. He lays his phone and bag on the counter.

JB's eyes lock on his mother's open opioid capsules.

JB
[What are these, Mama?]

JB'S MOTHER
[You know I need them for my back.]

JB
[But your surgery was 8 months ago.]

JB'S MOTHER
[JB, the doctor still prescribes them to me.]

JB, unconvinced, changes the subject.

JB
[We need to talk.]

JB'S MOTHER
[About what?]

JB
(placing the mail on the table)
[About these.]

JB's mother takes them and looks through them, cold and concerned.

JB (CONT'D)
[What's going on?]

JB'S MOTHER
[Your father is asking the judge to reevaluate the custody agreement between me and him over Mars.]

JB
(shocked)
[Naaah! Fuck that! How? They would really give Mars to that son of a bitch?]

JB'S MOTHER
[Hush! Don't speak like that about your father.]

JB
[How can you say that?! What he did to us! To you! He's not a father. A man who would do this to his own blood has no right being called that.]

JB rolls up his sleeve to show his scars.

JB'S MOTHER
["Who is a God like unto thee, that pardoneth iniquity, and passeth by the transgression of the remnant of his heritage? He re..."]

JB
(interrupting)
[Micah 7:18. Mom, how many verses are we gonna say? I prayed every day for him to change...]

JB's mother tries to cut him off in an endearing, quiet tone.

JB'S MOTHER
[JB...]

JB
(gesticulating his anger)
[EVERY DAY! Most days went unheard. Now you sayin for me to go back to that idle shit? Nah, I ain't playin that this time.]

JB'S MOTHER
[And do what!]
(beat)
[Leave him with no one?]

JB is silent.

JB'S MOTHER (CONT'D)
[The judge is requiring a reason for Mars staying with me, since your father...]
(beat)
[...is asking for partial custody. They say he got his act together with the youth ministries and fulfilling his parole.]

JB paces back and forth, apprehensive.

JB
[Can you preach when you the devil? What if I take guardianship?]

JB'S MOTHER
[How? You live here, and due to your history... the lawyers wrote that idea off.]

JB
(disgruntled)
[What we paying these motherfuckas for!?]

JB'S MOTHER
[Language!]
(taking a deep breath)
[Everything will be okay. God will protect us. There's a reason I got you and your brother those crosses.]
(beat)
[You still pray, don't you?]

JB starts looking at his phone after getting a notification.

JB
(annoyed)
[To who?]

JB's mother begins to speak in tongues.

JB
When you speak in tongues, I don't know what you're saying.

JB'S MOTHER
[Mars will stay with us. By God's will. Do you remember the verse I told you to read?]

JB
(doubtfully)
["Many are the afflictions of the righteous, but the Lord delivers them out of them all."]

JB'S MOTHER
[As God did then, He shall with us. Let's pray.]

She reaches for her holy oil, takes JB's phone and sets it to the side, then applies the oil to his forehead.

JB'S MOTHER (CONT'D)
[Dear Lord, I anoint your holy hands upon my son...]

JB's phone, set aside on the counter, glows with incoming texts.

INT. DANTE'S HOUSE - DAY

DANTE (22), Hispanic, wolf cut, is drawing with his deaf half-sister, TULA (12), Hispanic, straight brown hair. The doorbell rings. Dante gets up off the floor and heads for the door, passing a picture of himself, JB, and Mani. He looks through the peephole to find two well-dressed white women.

EXT. DANTE'S DOORSTEP - DAY

Dante opens the door to find JOANNE FARROW (mid 40s), white hair, slender, and BRIDGETTE PIERCE (mid 60s), brunette, a little overweight.

DANTE
(hesitantly)
Hello?

FARROW
Hello. Are you Dante Alvarez?

DANTE
Yeah.

FARROW
(reaching out her hand)
Nice to meet you. My name is Joanne, and this is my partner, Mrs. Pierce.

Dante stays quiet and looks at her hand.

FARROW (CONT'D)
Okay... We're from Child Protective Services, and we've been alerted about Tula Alvarez's care and needs. No need to be alarmed, we just have to conduct an inspection alongside some routine questions. Can we come in?

DANTE
(vexed)
Who alerted y'all?

PIERCE
We cannot disclose that information.

DANTE
Y'all can come in, but there ain't shit to find.

Pierce and Farrow step inside. Farrow closes the door behind her and smiles at Tula, who doesn't smile back.

TULA
(in sign language)
What's going on?

DANTE
(in sign language)
I don't know, but it will be fine... This will be a bore, so take my phone.

Pierce and Farrow check the rooms, the trash, the fridge, and the cabinets, writing what they observe in their notebooks. Dante walks over to the sitting area with them; Tula stays in the adjacent room, peeking at the conversation. Pierce lays out a clunky old laptop on the table.

.TULA'S POV - DANTE'S LIVING ROOM - DAY

NOTE: For the rest of this scene, lines marked TULA'S INTERPRETATION first appear on screen in braille, then decipher into English subtitles beneath -- Tula's reading of their lips. (__) marks words she misses, which stay in braille, undeciphered.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
So, as we said, we're just going to ask a couple questions. Everything should be smooth. Is that alright?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
Yeah.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Great. First, (__) full name, age, and occupation.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
My name is Dante Alvarez. I'm 22 years old, and (__), a cook at Vito's.

Pierce starts punching loud keys on the laptop.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Sorry for my colleague. She has her ways.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (PIERCE)
(jokingly)
I'm not with this whole "everything digital" landscape your generation is into.

Dante doesn't even crack a smile.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Bridgette, please. Don't worry, it won't interfere with the interview. Second question: how are you related to Tula?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
She's my half-sister.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
How long have you been her legal guardian?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
For about... 6 months, give or take.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Does Tula have access to adequate healthcare?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
Yes. I even pay out of pocket if something happens.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Is there any history of abuse or neglect in the home?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
No. I have never touched her, even when she go against what I say.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
How are you as a disciplinarian?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
I talk to her. Every time. She knows I don't judge her for what she does. If she punched a kid, they probably deserved that shit.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Is there any substance use in this household?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
No.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
How are you managing finances when it comes to her education, disability assistance, and overall needs?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
I'll admit it's tight, having to sacrifice one over the other, but I try, and she here healthy and happy. Most of my paycheck goes straight to providing her with what she needs.

The clacking of Pierce's laptop keys grows louder.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Final question: can you explain the police call made on May 28th?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
...If that was what y'all were getting at, y'all should have started with it.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Mr. Alvar--

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
My ex came over, we had a little altercation, and police had to arrive on scene.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (FARROW)
Okay. Now we just need a chat with Tula.

Dante motions for Tula to come over. She hesitantly does, and Tula and the CPS workers have a discussion. Afterward, Tula slips back into the adjacent room.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
Is that it?

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (PIERCE)
Yes, it is. Thank you. We came here today due to a report, and we'll have to weigh the information you gave us against it and pursue further steps on Tula's living arrangement. Would you like to fill out a survey on our performance and how CPS could better support you?

Dante stares at them blankly.

TULA'S INTERPRETATION (DANTE)
Yeah, I'm good off that. You can tell me who reported if you want to support.

Tula steps back in fear at Dante's response. Dante quickly glances toward the room Tula is in, giving her a look to reassure her.

INT. DANTE'S HOUSE - CONTINUOUS

PIERCE
Like we said, we cannot disclose that information.

DANTE
Y'all talking about foster homes and can't tell me who's trynna separate me from my sister.

PIERCE
Mr. Alvarez, the child's interests and needs are the priority. We play no sides.
(beat)
Thank you for your time. We will let you know our decision after further inspection.

Tula slowly comes out of the room as Dante walks them to the door. She can't make out what they're saying at the door. Dante belligerently shuts it and stands there for a few moments in disarray.

Tula comes up behind him. He sees her disconcerted face and uses his fingers to make a smile. She tries to make a stank face but falters at his charm.

Dante points to his locket. Tula points to hers. She smirks.

DANTE
(in sign language)
Mickey D's??

Tula smiles eagerly. Dante gets a text. As they walk out the door, we pass the picture of Dante, JB, and Mani -- taken in front of a diner.

FADE TO:

EXT. MEL'S DINER - DAY

Dante, JB, and Mani walk toward the restaurant through a parking lot full of Teslas, Hellcats, Hondas, and Toyotas. They dap each other up and head inside.

INT. MEL'S DINER - DAY

They take their seats at a table, jolly.

MANI
Shit, it's been a cool minute since we've all been here.

JB
For real.

A WAITRESS approaches the table.

WAITRESS
How are y'all doing today?

JB's eyes are stuck on the waitress.

JB
(flirtatiously)
We good now.

WAITRESS
Great to hear. Here's our menu! Just let me know if y'all need anything.

As the waitress walks away, JB checks out her body. Mani and Dante open the menu.

MANI
The fuck is this?

DANTE
20 bucks for a damn cheeseburger. My ass getting a kids menu. They got me fucked up.

Mani peeps JB staring at the waitress.

MANI
Nigga, she don't want yo ass.

JB
You saw how she looked at me.

MANI
She lookin for a tip.

JB
Nah, the eyes tell.

Mani shrugs the conversation off.

MANI
What y'all niggas been up to?

JB
Fuckin' bitches and gettin money.

Mani and Dante give him a blank look.

MANI
(to Dante, imitating)
What about you? Still sounding like a Mexican patriot?

They laugh.

DANTE
Just workin, for real.

The waitress brings an appetizer platter to the table.

MANI AND DANTE
(not in unison)
Thank you. / Appreciate it.

JB
Aye, what's your name?

WAITRESS
Demmy.

JB
Nice to meet you, Demmy. I saw you and thought you looked good. When you off, we should do sum.

DEMMY
Uhhh. That's nice of you, but I have a boyfriend.

Mani and Dante try to conceal their hysterical laughter.

JB
When that don't work out, hit me. You got IG?

DEMMY
(stepping away)
I don't have IG... sorry, I have to get back to work. Let me know if y'all want anything else.

JB looks at Dante and Mani, who can barely stay in their seats from laughing.

DANTE
(sarcastically)
The eyes tell?

MANI
(laughing)
She don't got IG. She might as well said "Ion run it."

JB
Fuck y'all.

DANTE
Aye, you miss the shots you don't take.

MANI
(eating)
How these years been treatin' y'all?

DANTE
Like shit.

JB
The most amount of truth I heard out of these two years.

MANI
Imma have to agree with y'all on that, though. But them stimulus checks.

DANTE
(reminiscent)
Shit's a blessing.

JB
(pointing to his Black Cat 4s)
When they deposited in my account, how fast my ass copped these.

DANTE
The Black Cats!!

MANI
Them jawns clean.

JB
(to Dante, dapping him up)
He knows! He knows! What you buy?

DANTE
Nothin. Straight to Tula.

JB
Crazy yo ass actually grew up.

DANTE
Had to someday.

MANI
Real shit. How's she doing?

DANTE
She good. She good.
(to Mani)
What about you?

MANI
Good. It's going... good.

JB
(gesturing an X to signify abortion)
Had to ask. You could have gone the...

DANTE
Or the milk option. Hood classic.

MANI
(jokingly)
True. Should I have hit Raley's or FoodMaxx?

They all laugh.

MANI (CONT'D)
All jokes aside. I'd be lying if it never crossed my mind.

JB
Grown man shit.

MANI
Had to step up.

DANTE
Grown man shit.

MANI
Aight nigga, we get it.
(to JB)
I know you up with the mom-and-pop shop.

JB
(eating)
That shit been gone.

JB doesn't look them in the eyes as he says it.

DANTE
Since when?

JB
Once the "panoramic" hit...

DANTE
Fuckkkkk. What about yo fam? How y'all gettin by?

JB
We sold the house. Well, it got foreclosed. Now we stay with some friends.

MANI
Damn.

JB
Dante, lighten the mood to this shit parade.

DANTE
Well, I got my sister back in my custody.

MANI
Aight, that's what we like to hear. Stackin yo shit up, I see.

DANTE
(tense)
Shit might change since these old white women came to my door with they bullshit.

A gloomy atmosphere takes hold of the table.

JB
Damn, some white niggas doin the same to me.

DANTE
Damn... we all got shit.

Silence permeates the air.

JB
So, to why I texted y'all. I been thinking about pulling something off... and seeing we all going through shit, more hands would help a whole lot.

MANI
This nigga wants me to end up in jail. You saying we steal?

JB
(mispronouncing it)
How you know? You clairvoyent or some shit?

DANTE
It's clairvoyant.

MANI
Nigga, I ain't dumb. Saw the newspaper about the bank shipment to town this week. Connected the dots that your ass would try to pull some GTA type shit.

JB
(hiding the newspaper in his bag)
Shiii. Well, that skips the bullshit of explaining it. Y'all in?

DANTE
STEAL! He said some GTA type shit, that doesn't mean we could pull off some GTA type shit.

JB
I have. All that's needed.

DANTE
(sarcastically)
You have. Didn't yo ass go to juvy... not one, not two, but three times?

JB
You talkin right now like I won't smack yo bitch ass.

Mani laughs.

DANTE
Try it, see what happens.

JB
Fuck is funny?

MANI
I'm in.

DANTE
(frustrated)
¡Gilipollas!

JB
(dapping Mani up and flipping off Dante)
Yessir! Love to hear it. Suck a dick.

DANTE
(looking down at his food)
Watch out for the booty warrior in prison!

MANI
If we...

DANTE
We?! You must be speaking French.

MANI
If... we doing this, we ain't robbing no bank.

JB
What you mean? Money is at the bank. Money waiting for us. We not hearing this.

MANI
Dante right. You don't got the best resume.

JB
I'm just catching strays here.

MANI
Nigga, if we go guns blazing with fucking masks like we out the Purge, we either getting locked up or getting put the fuck down.

JB starts listening and calms down.

MANI (CONT'D)
(trying to remember)
Remember Mr. Williams?

JB
Your film teacher?

MANI
Yeah, him. The equipment he got: Sony DSLRs, Canons, special edition lenses, filters, lights, a Blackmagic...

JB
English.

DANTE
Money.

MANI
A lot of money. I'm saying over 20k easily.

Dante and JB look lost, so Mani slows down.

MANI (CONT'D)
So if we steal the cameras, etch new serial numbers, pawn them off, and resell them for a marked-down price, we make bank. And the school district would reimburse him partly for the cameras, so his students could still use his equipment after we take they shit, if y'all didn't think about them.

DANTE
Ahhhhhhhh.

JB
You right.

MANI
So we in?

They all look at each other in affirmation.

EXT. HILL/OVERLOOK - NIGHT

Mani, JB, and Dante stand on top of a hill overlooking the school. JB hands the other two 9mm pistols.

MANI
What's this?

JB
Insurance.

MANI
We ain't gonna need this.

Mani tries to give the gun back, but JB pushes it back to him.

JB
Just take it.

MANI
Nigga...

JB
I ain't pulling no shit off without some insurance. Know better.

MANI
Aight, but no bodies. We ain't doing that.

JB
Hopefully Dante doesn't make bodies out of us. Mans don't know what the fuck the safety is.

Dante, looking over his 9mm, glares up.

DANTE
You always...

MANI
AYE.

Dante lets go of his anger and walks to the other side. JB smirks.

JB
Well, boys, to wish us luck and calm the nerves...

He takes a blunt out of his pocket.

MANI
Oh shiiit.

DANTE
Smokin before a heist... we goin to jail.

JB
Stop bitchin. It calms the nerves. KD smoke before games, helps with focus.

DANTE
Where you hear that from?

JB
Some nigga off TikTok.
(beat)
Am I smoking this myself...?

Mani takes a lighter out of his pocket. JB positions the blunt as Mani holds the lighter under it.

MANI
(motioning him over)
Dante.

Dante comes over and covers the lighter with his hands' warm embrace. From there, the trio passes the blunt around.

DANTE
So we doing this?

MANI
Yeah.

JB puts out the blunt. Mani puts on his mask, then JB, then Dante.

JB
What the fuck you wearing?

DANTE
My mask.

JB and Mani hold back their confusion and laughter at the sight. They cock their guns and start sneakily running toward the school.

EXT. SCHOOL CAMPUS - NIGHT

JB hops the fence, Mani after him with grace; Dante struggles over. They move slower now, checking their surroundings. JB starts to run for the building, but Dante pulls him back by the collar -- a JANITOR walks by on his nightly route.

They run quietly to the building's side door.

DANTE
Shi... locked.

MANI
No shit, Sherlock. You texted you had everything.

JB crouches down.

JB
(grinning)
I do.

He pulls a folded pick set from his hoodie sleeve, inserts the pick, and jiggles it with practiced rhythm.

Click. The lock gives.

MANI
NIGGA!

Mani and Dante look at him, stunned.

JB
What y'all think juvy was -- Boy Scouts?

JB pushes the door open and enters first. Mani and Dante follow.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - NIGHT

They step inside and freeze: a SECURITY CAMERA is mounted on the wall.

DANTE
Cameras!

JB
Fuck!

They press back to the edge of the corridor.

DANTE
When they get cameras?

MANI
Mr. Williams been had them. Bought them himself.

JB
What we doin?

Mani signals them to hush and points at the wall-mounted camera.

MANI
Look.

They watch the camera pan side to side.

DANTE
It moves.

JB
And?

MANI
Blind spot. If we're not in its line of sight...

JB
It won't see us.

MANI
Next time it moves to the right, stay close to the wall and move quick.

They wait. The lens glides. They bolt across, hugging the wall, to the equipment room door.

DANTE
Yo JB, can you pick this one?

JB scans the lock and shakes his head.

JB
Nah, this shit custom. Can't help on this one, y'all.

DANTE
So how the fuck we getting in?

JB clasps his hands like he's about to pray.

DANTE
The fuck is you doin?

JB
Get to prayin', nigga.

Mani smirks, already pulling a crowbar from his bag.

DANTE
Should've just said that.

Mani wedges it in the doorframe and uses his body weight to pry it open with a grunt. The door pops.

INT. EQUIPMENT ROOM - NIGHT

Shelves of cameras, lenses, and lights. They start loading their bags.

MANI
Be careful putting them in the bag.

JB
Nigga, I've done this more times than both y'all.

He fumbles a lens -- nearly drops it. Mani and Dante just stare.

A CLICK from the hallway door.

DANTE
What was that?

MANI
The janitor.

JB
Fuck.

MANI
Hurry this shit up.

They quickly stuff the cameras and equipment into their bags. Mani eyes the Blackmagic and motions toward it.

MANI (CONT'D)
I'll take this one.

He gently places the Blackmagic in his bag. They zip up.

MANI (CONT'D)
We good?

DANTE
Yeah.

JB
Yeah.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

They step out of the equipment room just as the hallway door unlocks -- the JANITOR catches them with duffel bags stuffed with stolen equipment. He's paralyzed.

JB takes a step toward the janitor and reveals his gun.

Mani sees JB reaching for his pistol and leaps first, knocking the janitor out. He looks at JB in disappointment.

They peek carefully out the door to make sure no one else is there, then run quickly and cheerfully through the hallways and hop the fence they came over, running away from the school. Then JB stops.

EXT. SIDEWALK - NIGHT

JB
I had that shit handled.

MANI
You call killing a man getting handled?!

JB
You coming at me right now?

MANI
WHAT I SAY? No bodies. And because one person saw us, you were gonna shoot 'em.

JB
A flesh wound. The fuck, kill him?

Mani walks away from the conversation in disagreement.

DANTE
Let's just get this shit back to the locker.

JB
Let's stop by the 7-Eleven first.

DANTE
You retarded?! We got stolen equipment in our bags.

JB
We got the shit. None of our faces are on camera, and do you hear that? No sirens. We straight. But imma need some bev after all that running.

DANTE
Nah, we going home.

JB
I'm going.

Dante points at the bag, moving to reach for it.

DANTE
Not with that bag.

JB clutches his duffel bag and steps up to Dante, fidgeting with his skull rings and exposing his gun.

JB
Or what? You gonna take it from me?

MANI
Y'all niggas need to chill out. We'll head to the gas station, JB gets his shit, and tomorrow we drop this shit off at Dante's work locker.

DANTE
Why don't we do this shit tonight?

MANI
I got somewhere to be later.

JB
Me too.

DANTE
You too? Fuck it.

EXT. GAS STATION - NIGHT

They arrive at the gas station. JB walks into the mart. Mani looks at his phone; Dante stands outside the glass window.

MANI
Stop looking sus and come inside.

They walk into the mart and see JB paralyzed in place.

INT. GAS STATION MART - CONTINUOUS

DANTE
Why aren't you...

They see why: a POLICE OFFICER checking out with a coffee. They freeze like JB.

In slow motion, the officer makes eye contact with them. He looks back as the CASHIER hands him his receipt, then looks at them again, innocently. The slow motion breaks when a call comes in over his radio. He walks toward them.

POLICE OFFICER
You boys look winded.

JB and Dante are too stunned to talk.

MANI
Yeah, we just finished running hurdles.

POLICE OFFICER
Hurdles. Such a difficult relay. Wish I could do that, but with these knees, you know. Hahahaha.

MANI
(nervously faking it)
I bet you still could. Hahaha.

POLICE OFFICER
Thanks. You boys must be tired. I'll let you be. Have a good evening.

MANI
You too, sir.

The officer gives them an assuring nod and exits. They all relax.

JB
Your white man voice suits you.

Mani aggressively side-eyes him.

DANTE
I told you we should have left!

MANI
Lower your voice. Too late now, we here.
(to JB)
Hurry up and get yo shit.

JB
Aight, aight.

JB goes to the drink section, then quickly to the card aisle.

Three MASKED ROBBERS walk into the mart in a triangle formation, each unveiling a 9mm pistol. ROBBER 1 and ROBBER 2 move up to the register; ROBBER 3, carrying a black duffel bag, moves into the aisles.

ROBBER 1
This a stick up.

Robber 2 goes to the cashier and hits him on top of the head.

ROBBER 2
Empty the bag, nigga. You know how this shit goes.

Robber 3 walks up to Dante and Mani.

ROBBER 3
What y'all niggas got in the bag?

MANI
Our track clothes.

ROBBER 3
Hahaha. Y'all think I'm stupid. Empty the bag.

Mani stands still and stares at him.

ROBBER 3 (CONT'D)
You think I'm playing?

He raises his gun to Mani's temple.

ROBBER 3 (CONT'D)
I ain't gonna repeat myself.

JB peeks out of the card aisle and sneaks past the boys. He fires the first shot -- and misses. Mani and Dante scatter for cover.

Robber 1 returns fire. Robber 2 parkours over the register and starts shooting. Robber 3, in the aisles, shoots at Dante and Mani.

Dante fumbles a fresh magazine into his pistol, then fires erratically with no clear direction. In the middle of the shooting, Mani takes aim at Robber 3, takes a deep breath, and fires one shot.

CASHIER
AHHHHHH!

Someone shoots out the lights. Shots are fired in the dark.

EXT. GAS STATION - NIGHT

Muzzle flashes illuminate the windows, until no motion is left inside.

ALICIA (V.O.)
Mani, we're almost here and still no text from you. Where yo ass at? I swear if you flake this motherfuckin time, you'll have other shit to think about than those damn bills. Run yo ass here.

EXT. GAS STATION - LATER

Police cars have swarmed the gas station.

INT. GAS STATION MART - CONTINUOUS

Forensics seals off evidence. Everyone lies dead in their own blood. The police officer from earlier looks around and sees the young men he talked to, lifeless on the grimy floor.

Forensics collects the black duffel bag from the robbers and takes out extra clips, money, Pampers diapers, and a notebook. As they work, Mani's phone plays "Honey, It's Alright" by Gregory Alan Isakov. A forensics tech walks past JB, still holding a bloody "14th" birthday card in his left hand. Dante's necklace beads are scattered across the floor; the locket is bagged by forensics.

INT. MS. G'S HOUSE - NIGHT

JB's mother and Ms. G talk worriedly beside a cake with candles, next to a half-wrapped new FIFA game. Mars sits at the table, waiting for his brother. Through the window, three red crosses glow.

INT. DANTE'S HOUSE - NIGHT

Tula sleeps with her locket on.

INT. ICE CREAM SHOP - NIGHT

Through the glass of an ice cream shop: Alicia and Celine. Alicia viciously texts Mani under the table. Cop cars race by outside; she watches them until Celine pulls her attention back by getting ice cream on her mouth.

CELINE
Where's Daddy?

ALICIA
(wiping her mouth)
He'll be here soon, sweetie.

> END <
